<urn:atm:triage:finding/BA3-QA1-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BA3-QA1-004" ;
  triage:title "Task 4's documented no-delivery-channel Hold behavior is not implemented anywhere; its only test is one of the hollow BA3-QA1-002 aliases" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (req-qa), PR #1402 @ c13f9bddf, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1402#issuecomment-5643113496. Task 4's documented behavior (Hold(\"no delivery channel\"), one warn per tick) is not implemented anywhere: build_task_reminder_dispatch's Ok(None) case is a bare return with no disposition or log line, and no \"no delivery channel\" string exists in the crate. Its supposed test, member_without_dispatchable_backend_holds_and_logs_once, is one of the hollow aliases from BA3-QA1-002, so this gap shipped undetected. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1402#issuecomment-5643134050): STANDS; folded into BA3-FIX-R3-1789183410 with its test." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
